# Copy to .env.local for local overrides. Neither variable is needed to run the
# app locally — the defaults already point at the API on :8000.
#
# Both are read at BUILD time, not run time: they are compiled into the bundle
# and the route manifest, so changing either means a rebuild/redeploy.

# Where the browser sends API calls. Absolute means it talks to the API
# directly, and the API must list this app's origin in ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-api.onrender.com/api/v1

# The alternative: leave NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL set to /api/v1 (relative) and set
# API_ORIGIN instead. Next then proxies /api/v1/* to the backend from the
# server, so the browser only ever talks to this origin and CORS never applies.
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api/v1
# API_ORIGIN=https://your-api.onrender.com
